  "name": "MOSS-Image",
  "description": "**MOSS-Image** — the fully open text-to-image model (Apache 2.0, commercial use allowed) that lets you *place* things instead of just describing them.\n\n- **Layout control**: draw bounding boxes and say what goes in each one — characters, products and text land exactly where you put them\n- **Typography that reads**: posters, memes, signs and labels with the words spelled right\n- **Prompt weighting** `(phrase:1.3)`: crank an idea up, or weight it negative to erase it from the image\n- **Runs on 12 GB**: the INT8 ConvRot build on every tier — blind-tested against the full BF16 model, same look, about 25% faster\n- Needs ComfyUI 0.42 or newer (installed fresh from master)\n\nIncludes three workflows by **IntoTheLatent**: **Text2Image Simple**, **Bounding Boxes** (layout prompt builder + style wizard) and **Batch Prompt**.",
